  "id": "hysterical-paralysis",
  "term": "hysterical paralysis",
  "definition": "Hysterical paralysis is a historical term for a loss of movement seen in hysteria that was described as not arising from structural paralysis in the usual organic sense. In this account, it is marked by failure to make effective effort despite some preserved muscle tone, and it may appear alongside or reinforce an existing bodily illness.",
